    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Lawrence Butler** (74.61) and **Dylan Beavers** (69.52) headline our offensive output, both benefiting significantly from a soft matchup against Nick Martinez and Ober, respectively. **Butler**\u2019s massive 13% platoon edge and favorable park factors make him our premier start, while **Beavers** gains a crucial efficiency boost from an aggressive base-stealing environment against a pitcher with a notoriously slow delivery\u2014a priority metric for our squad. **Jonathan Aranda** (68.94) rounds out our top trio, as his projected #2 spot in the order paired with a +12% dynamic platoon advantage positions him perfectly to capitalize on Mason Barnett\u2019s shaky 4.10 xERA. We are leaning heavily into these high-floor, high-upside matchups to drive our scoring across the 5x5 categories.\n\nOur bench optimization was razor-thin today, with **Daulton Varsho** (54.44) narrowly missing the cut behind **Cal Raleigh**. While **Varsho** offers elite versatility, the optimizer favored **Raleigh** due to a more favorable individual platoon matchup against Weathers; **Varsho**\u2019s efficiency was dragged down by a -10% penalty for his current dynamic platoon standing. Elsewhere, we remain cautious regarding **JJ Bleday** and **Braden Montgomery**, both of whom are sidelined by a combination of low-ceiling metrics and a 33% rain risk that introduces unnecessary volatility. We are currently playing the \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Yainer Diaz**, **Zack Gelof**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Luis Arraez**, **Kyle Karros**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Justin Crawford**, and **Bryce Harper**; these projections assume aggressive middle-to-top-of-the-order placements, and we will monitor confirmed lineups to ensure our speed-first strategy remains intact.",
